ay I think they don't give a message  specifically then what kind of  evangelical in that way or even like an  academic work saying you know this is  how it is what you hope of you will do  is to travel with you with your sense of  sort of exploration in country after  country and I hope what they would take  away it would be obvious enjoyment and  the sense of of energy the  extraordinaire nests of this route and  the relevance obviously of those  countries that it's left behind in  particular now Afghanistan Iran Central  Asia these countries would have suddenly  become important to us how long did the  journey take you it only took me eight  months people are often surprised by  this because it seemed a long and I was  it was held up at times by fighting in  Afghanistan fighting between warlords I  mean and by the SAS fathers in China I  was quality in force on the edge of the  Chinese desert so it took me a little  over eight months in all do you know how  long it would have taken someone  centuries ago to make the journey it  would of course nobody did the entire  journey or almost never and I guess if  you had wanted to do it in a good camel  train it would taken you a year and a  half something like that but the times  always varied and the goods as I say  were constantly exchanging hands and  sort of relay race so nobody ever did it  from them from the China Sea to the  Mediterranean did to them and what is  your background well I I don't have an  academic background I was fascinated by  writing as a child my father was an Army  officer and so I was used to travel even  as a child he was a military attache in  Ottawa worked in the States  and as a child as a post war child in  England coming to the states and to  Canada was amazing I've never even seen  a neon light before and suddenly I was  in New York in time of squares and ATOL  completely dazzled and I think something  of that fascinate  with the wonders of abroad and a  movement of travel stayed with me always  so when I when I sort of left school I  went into publishing for a few years and  then I just took the risk to like to  travel which was on Damascus in those  days back in the 60s nothing thank you  so much mister the run  thank you very much for more information  about the book TV bus visit our website  at book TV org slash book TV bus here's  a look at some upcoming book fairs and  festivals next week

